{"name":"Spa Dream","hex":"#1993be","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spa","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Spanish."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A health resort near a mineral spring or hot spring.","A trendy or fashionable resort."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spa"},{"term":"dream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Imaginary events seen in the mind while sleeping.","A hope or wish."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To see imaginary events in one's mind while sleeping.","To hope, to wish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spa","blocks":[{"text":"A spa is a location where mineral-rich spring water is used to give medicinal baths. Spa health treatments are known as balneotherapy. The belief in the curative powers of mineral waters and hot springs goes back to prehistoric times. Spa towns, spa resorts, and day spas are popular worldwide, but are especially widespread in Europe and Japan. Bathing regimens in ancient Greece formed the foundation for modern spa procedures. Following a decline in public bathing during medieval times, spas became popular health resorts and social centers for the upper class in the 18th century."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Medicinal_spa_of_Hark%C3%A1ny.jpg/330px-Medicinal_spa_of_Hark%C3%A1ny.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spa"},{"title":"Dream","blocks":[{"text":"A dream is a succession of images, dynamic scenes and situations, ideas, emotions, and sensations that usually occur involuntarily in the mind during certain stages of sleep. Humans generally spend more than two hours dreaming per night, and each dream lasts around 5–20 minutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg/330px-A_dream_%28BM_